00:11.070 --> 00:15.210
Installing Git on a Windows machine is, it's not complicated

00:15.210 --> 00:18.210
but it's a little bit trickier than to do it on a Mac.

00:18.210 --> 00:20.370
And the reason for this is that Git was designed,

00:20.370 --> 00:23.490
it was created, if you watch that video where I did

00:23.490 --> 00:25.320
you know, the brief history of Git,

00:25.320 --> 00:28.200
it was created to run on a Unix-based interface.

00:28.200 --> 00:31.620
It was designed for Linux because the guy who created it

00:31.620 --> 00:34.620
Linus Torvalds, also created Linux.

00:34.620 --> 00:38.370
Okay, the problem that we run into on a Windows machine

00:38.370 --> 00:40.350
is that Windows machines

00:40.350 --> 00:44.010
don't come with a Unix-based prompt by default.

00:44.010 --> 00:46.470
Windows comes with a different command line interface

00:46.470 --> 00:48.510
called Command Prompt.

00:48.510 --> 00:49.650
It's not Unix-based.

00:49.650 --> 00:50.670
If you don't know what Unix is,

00:50.670 --> 00:52.230
it really it's not a big deal.

00:52.230 --> 00:53.790
You don't need to know what it is.

00:53.790 --> 00:55.470
It just causes an issue here.

00:55.470 --> 00:58.170
Git wants to run with a Unix-based interface

00:58.170 --> 00:59.280
and there's this shell,

00:59.280 --> 01:02.070
this thing called Bash that is a default shell

01:02.070 --> 01:03.780
for Linux machines and for Macs.

01:03.780 --> 01:05.370
So it's a lot easier on those machines.

01:05.370 --> 01:07.260
We don't have to go jump through any hoops.

01:07.260 --> 01:08.550
On a Windows machine,

01:08.550 --> 01:11.250
we have to download something called Git Bash

01:11.250 --> 01:13.650
which we're about to do and Git Bash

01:13.650 --> 01:16.650
is going to emulate a Bash, a Unix experience

01:16.650 --> 01:18.150
on our Windows machine.

01:18.150 --> 01:20.190
And it comes with Git also.

01:20.190 --> 01:22.260
So some people actually use Git Bash

01:22.260 --> 01:24.120
without even touching the Git portion.

01:24.120 --> 01:26.100
They just want the Bash portion.

01:26.100 --> 01:28.800
Anyway, you'll see, you know, it's not too bad

